{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4729",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to bind to Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, both of which participate in Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity, which is then participated by Ndufv2. This suggests a potential mechanism by which Metformin may influence Ndufv2 through its interaction with Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, which are subunits of the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex. The shared involvement of Ndufa12 and Ndufv3 in the same activity implies that Metformin may modulate the activity of this complex, potentially affecting its function in cellular respiration. The high scores from the three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Metformin and Ndufv2, suggesting that the observed interactions are biologically relevant. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of Nadh Dehydrogenase activity, which could have downstream effects on energy metabolism and cellular function. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Metformin and Ndufv2 through its influence on the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of this interaction.",
